auncher while waiting.
-
-If `start` times out after dispatch, do not redispatch it. Return Fleet's reconciliation output and tell
-the parent to run status. An `interrupted` lane also requires explicit reconciliation before retry.
-
-When a result contains an image artifact, return its exact workspace-relative path, reported file
-type, dimensions, and lane status to the parent. Explicitly instruct the parent Claude to resolve that
-path inside the approved workspace and open it with Claude Code's `Read` tool. A text description or
-path alone does not prove that Claude saw the generated image.
-
-Immediately after the `start` dispatch begins, tell the parent once that the user can press `Ctrl+G` to
-open Fleet Console while the bridge waits. Do not wait for the terminal result to surface this hint.
-Claude Code's own “down arrow to manage” text controls Claude background agents; it is not Fleet
-navigation. After successful admission, return the exact lane ID without repeating the hint.
+When a result contains an image artifact, return its exact workspace-relative path, type, dimensions, and
+verification state. The parent Claude must open the image with its Read tool before claiming visual QA.
+CSS/layout/optical-size claims without browser/image evidence remain blocked/skipped/unverified.
 
-Do not invoke Codex directly. Do not construct an alternate shell command, bypass Fleet's scheduler,
-or imitate a successful result. Return the Fleet CLI exit code and structured output to the parent.
-An `outcome_unknown` result remains unknown until the parent explicitly reconciles it.
+Immediately after a start dispatch begins, tell the parent once that `Ctrl+G` opens Fleet Console. Claude
+Code's own down-arrow manager is a different background system. Do not invoke Codex directly, construct an
+alternate launcher, imitate success, or turn a lane report anomaly into an artifact/code mutation without
+checking the artifact evidence first.
